WEBVTT

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.960
<i>There, in that world, he listened 
to the sound of bubbles being born,</i>

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:11.590
This story is a work of fiction. All persons and organizations are imagined. 
The kabaddi and game rules which appear in this anime are drawn from the original work.

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:11.370
<i>he heard the sound of water splitting open...</i>

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.780
<i>and, in the end, he heard voices cheering.</i>

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:19.290
<i>That was how Takaya Ren, who knew what 
it was to be number one, spent his days.</i>

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.790
Ren-kun!

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.920
<b>Raider
Souwa Takaya</b>

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.920
<b>Souwa      Noukin</b>

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.920
<b>Defense
Noukin 5 players</b>

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:29.020
Kabaddi.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.420
If we can stop him here, it'll be huge!

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.340
Yeah!

00:02:03.550 --> 00:02:09.150
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:08.710
<i>Chase X
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hCounterattack</i>

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:07.180
<i>We haven't built up momentum yet.</i>

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.950
<i>First, we need to crush 
the cat-eyed jerk.</i>

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.980
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:15.150
<i>He really is fast!</i>

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:15.990
<i>But...</i>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.070
<i>not as fast as our captain!</i>

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:20.990
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:22.780
<i>Where do you think you're looking?!</i>

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:24.630
Idiot! That's way too 
close to enemy territory!

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.250
No. He hasn't noticed!

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:30.880
Kabaddi!

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:33.130
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:34.750
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:35.890
<i>He can make it back!</i>

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:37.460
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:38.840
<i>Why is he headed deeper?</i>

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:39.970
Stop him, Yoigoshi!

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:44.470
<b>Bonus Line</b>

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:42.040
We have five on defense right now!

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.470
He's trying to get another point 
by crossing the bonus line!

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:45.900
<i>Bonus!</i>

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.230
So that's what it was!

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:52.060
Kabaddi...

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:52.060
We're gonna make you drop all 
the points you're holding!

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:54.750
Kabaddi!

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:56.300
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.680
<i>If we take him down, this won't matter!</i>

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:00.420
<i>Huh?</i>

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.360
<i>What?</i>

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.620
<i>He went outside the court?</i>

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:15.750
<b>Souwa    Noukin</b>

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:18.270
You left the court!

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.590
He only touched the ground 
within his territory.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:21.720
The points count.

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:26.370
One point for crossing the bonus line. 
Three points by touching.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.640
That's four points total!

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:30.940
I'm tired of hearing it.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:35.440
I'm tired of hearing the complaints of 
losers and the cheers of the crowd.

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.400
<i>Losers?</i>

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.530
This is how you use long arms and legs.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.950
You shouldn't be satisfied 
with just three points.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:48.450
<b>OUT: Yoigoshi, Misumi, Iura</b>

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:47.740
We're out. We need to 
leave the court, Yoigoshi.

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:52.960
The way he looks down on us! We need 
to get points on the raid again!

00:03:54.940 --> 00:03:57.100
Wait, we don't have a raider 
on the court right now!

00:03:58.690 --> 00:03:59.670
I'll go.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:00.730
What?

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:03.200
It's normal to be nervous your first match.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.570
He's the weird one.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.640
<b>Defense
Souwa 5 players</b>

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:08.640
<b>Raider
Noukin / Date</b>

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.100
Kabaddi.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.850
That guy's got a good build.

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.440
Don't be intimidated. 
We've got five on defense here.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:19.200
Yeah. Those are the footsteps 
of someone with no speed.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.090
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.660
<i>I'll stop him.</i>

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.160
<i>And I'll leave the rest to you!</i>

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.860
Kabaddi!

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.030
Seriously?

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.160
Whoa!

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:31.390
He's flailing all over the place. 
There's no way to get close to that.

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:33.160
Come on! Somebody, hurry up!

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:34.840
Yes.

00:04:35.990 --> 00:04:37.050
Leave it to me!

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:44.170
Wow! That looked so easy!

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:46.720
Nice anti, Captain Rokugen!

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.680
He got Shin... with just one hand?

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.490
Number four, out!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.310
<b>Souwa    Noukin</b>

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.310
<b>Raid Failed: Date OUT
Souwa: 1 point Gained</b>

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:53.810
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.810
<i>Failing to get Takaya out was bad,</i>

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:00.450
<i>but to have our strongest power player 
taken down with one hand...</i>

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:01.990
<i>that's rough, psychologically.</i>

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.090
<i>Is this what you were aiming for, Rokugen?</i>

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:07.570
Still, you have quite an impressive physique.

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:10.700
You must have put yourself through 
an immense amount of training.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:11.780
Thank you.

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:14.080
<i>I guess he's not really the type.</i>

00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:18.580
The only shame is that it isn't 
a physique built for kabaddi yet.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:21.310
You cannot win with brute strength alone.

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.570
I know that from experience.

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:28.780
Every single one of them is just...

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.810
Calm down. We need to do this rationally.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.780
You, too, Azemichi! You're alone 
out there, but stay calm!

00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:36.060
S-Sir!

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:39.750
What happens if everyone is out? Do we lose?

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.620
We don't lose, but it's called a "lona,"

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:48.860
<b>"Lona"</b>

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:47.180
and in exchange for everyone returning to 
the court, the other team gets two points.

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.860
They get another two points?

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.820
<b>Raider
Souwa / Takaya</b>

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.820
<b>Defense
Noukin / Azemichi</b>

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:50.820
Make sure you stop him, 
Azemichi!

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.870
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.380
He's completely tensed up.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:06:00.890
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.370
It's because it's his first match.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.880
And just playing one-on-one 
in itself is rough.

00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:05.380
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:08.300
<i>Am I going to be able to take 
this guy down one-on-one?</i>

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:10.710
<i>A guy so big and so fast...</i>

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:13.660
Kabaddi!

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:16.810
<i>What?</i>

00:06:17.220 --> 00:06:19.310
<i>This is just the same as usual!</i>

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:20.730
Looks like he's back.

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.320
He's moving well, don't you think?

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:25.980
When you're short, having a shorter 
reach is a disadvantage,

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:29.360
but since your center of gravity is stable, 
there's strength in even the small movements.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.270
Most importantly,

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:32.660
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:32.660
when you're in a low position, it isn't easy 
for a raider to go in for a touch.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:37.180
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:06:33.180 --> 00:06:36.830
They run the risk that their legs, 
their lifeline, will be caught.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.900
So, even though Azemichi's on his own,
 if he can grab Takaya's legs...

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:41.550
That's right. He can take him down.

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:44.360
Plus, they're playing one-on-one. 
There's only one target.

00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:47.420
Kabaddi, Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:06:45.050 --> 00:06:47.420
Takaya will fight deep in the court.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:51.450
<i>If we were to show this situation 
another way, it would be... iai!</i>

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:53.400
<i>Each is trying to finish the 
other with a single killer blow.</i>

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.790
<i>No help is coming.</i>

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.720
This scenario is one I've already thought of.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:00.600
A leg-tackle from a low position.

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.730
I had Azemichi practice that exhaustively.

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:07.240
Even as he slammed his head into my knees, 
he did it over and over again.

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:08.780
Kabaddi.

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.810
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.190
<i>He's mine!</i>

00:07:18.130 --> 00:07:19.830
<i>His weight disappeared?</i>

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:20.840
<i>It can't be!</i>

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.170
Kabaddi!

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.050
<i>He shook him off?!</i>

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:30.700
Kabaddi.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.800
Souwa, raid successful!

00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:38.340
And I'll take the 
two-point lona, too, thanks!

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.690
<b>"Lona"
Noukin High School Wiped Out</b>

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.690
<i>Noukin High School, lona.</i>

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:46.650
<b>Souwa: Takaya Raid Successful
Touch 1 pt + Lona 2 pts
3 pts Gained</b>

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:49.980
H-His reaction was insane...

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:52.290
You predicted that was coming, didn't you?

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:58.160
'Course I did! That catch was so sharp, 
I figured you must've practiced a ton.

00:07:58.800 --> 00:08:02.540
That's why I dove deeper 
instead of dodging. Okay?

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:04.280
Yeah.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:05.890
It wasn't bad,

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:09.140
but anyone who gets taken down 
by that is still second-rate.

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:12.510
<b>Previously taken down by that</b>

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:16.010
<i>Takaya Ren. He's definitely first-rate.</i>

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:20.520
<i>Deliberately crushing our strong points 
to show the difference in ability...</i>

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:24.510
The momentum Yoigoshi created 
has completely disappeared.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:28.020
<i>After that, the point 
spread continued to grow.</i>

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:30.260
This isn't good.

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:32.530
A ten-point spread. Is that bad?

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:34.960
Having lots of points taken at once is bad.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:37.530
We've lost antis, so we're still 
at a disadvantage in numbers.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.540
When fewer players on defense, 
you can't stop raids you normally could.

00:08:42.010 --> 00:08:44.010
First, let's get our stances solid.

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:46.110
Yoigoshi, your match with 
Takaya will have to—

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:46.920
I know!

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:49.720
There's no point if we lose the match.

00:08:49.720 --> 00:08:50.550
I'll be back.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.550
Kabaddi!

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.570
Will he target Takaya again?

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:56.080
Look at him, all fired up.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:56.940
Kabaddi!

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.250
<i>He's fast!</i>

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:01.810
<i>But rashly traveling deep 
into the court is reckless.</i>

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:04.890
<i>A five-man defense can easily cut 
off a raider's lines of escape!</i>

00:09:05.790 --> 00:09:07.060
<i>And we're done here.</i>

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:09.740
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:07.950 --> 00:09:09.740
<i>Your retreat has been blocked off.</i>

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:10.440
Kabaddi!

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:12.440
Wasn't he gunning for Takaya?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.860
<i>If a single blow isn't enough 
to create momentum for us,</i>

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:16.950
<i>then first, I'll reduce their defense!</i>

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.750
There's nowhere to run!

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.190
No, he's got reach! Watch the outside!

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.390
<i>The outside, you say?</i>

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:23.960
<i>For me...</i>

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.020
<i>there's this!</i>

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:27.500
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:09:28.010 --> 00:09:29.790
That's something we're used to seeing.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:30.980
A feint, huh?

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:33.010
Without a ball, he's even faster!

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:40.010
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:35.730
<i>Okay. That's two out.</i>

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.420
<i>We'll have all our members on defense.</i>

00:09:37.420 --> 00:09:39.000
<i>We can start over from here.</i>

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.010
<i>Just watch, Takaya.</i>

00:09:41.910 --> 00:09:43.060
<i>Where'd he go?</i>

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:45.480
<b>Souwa      Noukin</b>

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:43.580
Kabaddi...

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:44.860
At any rate, that's two points!

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:47.480
Hurry up and come back, Yoigoshi!

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:48.510
Huh?

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:49.940
Kabaddi!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.480
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:09:51.690 --> 00:09:54.250
As soon as you came back, 
it was their turn to raid!

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:55.200
Wha—?!

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.420
<i>He...</i>

00:09:56.420 --> 00:09:58.680
<i>He was right behind me?!</i>

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:00.050
<i>This is bad.</i>

00:10:00.050 --> 00:10:02.700
<i>At this rate, it's the same 
as playing four-on-one!</i>

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:05.700
<i>Plus, Misumi and Azemichi 
only just came back!</i>

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:06.950
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.470
<i>Our defense is all over the place!</i>

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:11.000
Kabaddi...

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:15.350
<i>What is this?</i>

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:17.170
<b>Souwa      Noukin</b>

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:17.170
<b>Souwa: Takaya Raid Successful
Touch 3 pts Gained</b>

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:21.180
<b>OUT: Yoigoshi, Iura, Date</b>

00:10:17.510 --> 00:10:18.730
That's three points!

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:21.180
Noukin's only got two 
players left until a lona!

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:23.230
Nice chase!

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.130
"Chase"?

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:27.030
An attack strategy where, as soon 
as we returned to our territory,

00:10:27.030 --> 00:10:29.360
they attacked with no time gap.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:30.770
Is that allowed?

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:33.770
As long as the raider hasn't been tackled 
when returning to home territory,

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.360
there's no rule against it.

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:39.450
You have to get close to the raider as they 
head back, so there's risk to it, too.

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:42.110
I see!

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:43.950
If I'd been more guarded about my rear,

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:44.750
Yikes!

00:10:43.950 --> 00:10:47.120
it might have been possible for me 
to touch him right before returning!

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:48.760
Damn it!

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:51.180
I'm sorry. I should have 
taught you about that.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:55.630
<i>He timed his attack for the 
moment we were trying to start over.</i>

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:56.630
<i>He really is a nasty one.</i>

00:10:57.260 --> 00:11:00.750
<i>And the ones he touched were our 
raider-types, me and Yoigoshi.</i>

00:11:00.750 --> 00:11:03.100
<i>Plus, Date, who raided once.</i>

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.600
<b>Defense
Souwa 5 Players</b>

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:06.600
<b>Raider
Noukin / Misumi</b>

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:05.590
<i>He's killed our offense.</i>

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:09.100
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:11.590
Kabaddi! Kabaddi!

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:13.770
<i>All of them are pretty well built!</i>

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:16.320
<i>And the second I take my eye 
off them, they circle around!</i>

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.370
Kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:19.700
<b>Misumi Returns: No Points</b>

00:11:17.340 --> 00:11:19.700
Blast! Their defense is too tight!

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:21.530
<i>He wasn't able to score, huh?</i>

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:25.730
Just don't get caught! See the defense 
through with just the two of you!

00:11:26.510 --> 00:11:27.410
Sir!

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:30.220
Defense is our domain!

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:32.620
We're stopping them, 
even if we're up against Takaya!

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:33.630
Sir!

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:39.490
<i>Rokugen is... the raider?!</i>

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.080
This guy can raid, too?

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:49.680
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:46.180
They're keeping Takaya-san in reserve?

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:49.090
This guy's got power, Azemichi!

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:50.200
Sir!

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:51.290
Kabaddi!

00:11:52.510 --> 00:11:55.190
<i>Stop his legs! That's all I can think about!</i>

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:57.180
Kabaddi...

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:59.070
<i>He's coming.</i>

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:00.660
<i>He dodged?</i>

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:03.410
Rokugen.

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:04.490
Damn it...

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:11.990
Kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:08.490
<i>He can dodge Azemichi's catch
with that huge build?</i>

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.540
<i>His cant and his movements are steady.</i>

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:14.200
Kabaddi, kabaddi!

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:19.000
Azemichi!

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:22.010
Kabaddi...

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.220
He grabbed him!

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:25.220
<i>This guy...</i>

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:27.540
<i>It doesn't matter how many times you dodge!</i>

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:29.510
<i>I'll stop your legs! That's all!</i>

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:33.060
Kabaddi!

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:35.560
<i>Letting them catch me. Pathetic.</i>

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:38.780
<i>If I had the same build as Ojo, 
they would have taken me down.</i>

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.980
<i>Still lacking...</i>

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:43.570
<i>I'm still sorely lacking!</i>

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:45.430
<i>Even though I've got his leg...</i>

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:47.570
<i>Even though there's two of us on him!</i>

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:48.730
Kabaddi.

00:12:49.580 --> 00:12:52.580
Two points! Noukin, lona!

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.410
Two additional points to Souwa!

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.920
<b>Souwa: Rokugen Raid Successful</b>

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.920
<b>Touch 2 pts + Lona 2 pts
= 4 pts Gained</b>

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:01.370
That's our second...

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:02.920
...lona.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:06.930
A fifteen-point spread. 
We have to get those back, or else...

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:09.900
Splash.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:11.520
<i>Noukin.</i>

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:16.480
<i>Facing their second lona of the day, 
their mental state has taken a deep plunge.</i>

00:13:17.650 --> 00:13:19.380
Referee, time out!

00:13:19.380 --> 00:13:20.420
We're switching players.

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:27.680
I-I'm fine! This'll stop in no time!

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:28.580
I can still—

00:13:28.580 --> 00:13:29.490
Soma.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:32.620
Injuries are just as terrifying as defeat.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.810
Make sure you get that treated properly.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:38.050
Noukin, member change!

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.440
Azemichi...

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:43.050
I'm fine! The cut I got from 
practice opened up, that's all.

00:13:44.060 --> 00:13:45.510
Thank you. I'm ready to play.

00:13:46.390 --> 00:13:49.010
We'll resume play with Noukin raiding!

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:51.970
That guy is...

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:53.660
Noukin's captain and...

00:13:54.990 --> 00:13:57.560
He's here! He's here, Rokugen-san!

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:58.500
Watch.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:13:59.070
Huh?

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:02.150
I said don't take your eyes off him!

00:14:02.430 --> 00:14:05.710
<i>Don't worry. I'm making sure to listen, so—</i>

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:06.650
Kabaddi.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.370
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.650
<i>The sound... I mean...</i>

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:19.990
Kabaddi.

00:14:26.780 --> 00:14:30.180
F-Four points to Noukin.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:32.970
Huh? I thought I had crossed the bonus line.

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.180
You did!

00:14:36.920 --> 00:14:37.930
I thought so.

00:14:37.930 --> 00:14:41.080
I wouldn't be satisfied 
with just four points.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.440
<b>Noukin: Ojo Raid Successful
Bonus 1 pt + Touch 4 pts
 5 pts Gained</b>

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.440
Five points! And on top of that...

00:14:45.050 --> 00:14:46.780
he sent Takaya out!

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:50.200
H-He got five points?!

00:14:53.110 --> 00:14:54.700
Takaya-san...

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.480
This is the first time he's 
been outside the court!

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:00.870
It's like he appeared out of nowhere...

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:02.540
You thought so, too?

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:06.000
That was a fun raid.

00:15:06.400 --> 00:15:08.380
Well, shall we get on defense?

00:15:09.530 --> 00:15:10.640
Captain!

00:15:10.640 --> 00:15:12.230
It's too early to be happy.

00:15:12.230 --> 00:15:14.800
Let's crush Rokugen and get a lona.

00:15:15.020 --> 00:15:15.990
Yeah!

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:23.690
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:21.580
<i>Is he smiling?</i>

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:23.340
<i>If he gets taken down, it's a lona.</i>

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:27.770
<i>I should have the advantage in speed. 
I'll draw him deep into the court.</i>

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:26.760
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:27.770 --> 00:15:28.690
Kabaddi.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:30.860
<i>The same as the captain?</i>

00:15:31.170 --> 00:15:32.060
<i>That was close!</i>

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:36.080
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:36.080
<i>I can't sense anything. 
It's hard to read him!</i>

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:38.770
Kabaddi!

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:41.420
Rokugen, you've changed.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.580
You're no longer all about power.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:45.440
He's good at circling around!

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:47.840
He's built so slim, 
and he goes in that boldly?

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:49.810
I'll draw him in.

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:53.710
If three, no, four of us don't go in at once, 
tackling will be too dangerous.

00:15:53.710 --> 00:15:54.930
Four of us?

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.950
<i>There is no need for that.</i>

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:59.890
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:02.020
H-He went back?

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:05.020
We're not in the struggle, right?

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:08.230
Souwa, bonus point gained!

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:10.720
Blast! He'd crossed the bonus line?

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:13.670
Huh? Wait... When it's 
just the bonus, then...

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.720
They get one point, that's all.

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:19.170
No one is out, and none of 
their players come back.

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:21.790
Why'd he do that? Did he just get 
tired of attacking and head back?

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:25.690
Rokugen, that wasn't good, as a captain.

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:28.090
Do you really want to play 
me one-on-one that badly?

00:16:29.160 --> 00:16:30.920
This is the only opportunity.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:35.080
The players outside the court will come 
back in the order they were tagged out.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:39.560
If I send a single player out, my chance 
to play you one-on-one disappears.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.870
It's been about three years now...

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.560
Ever since we parted ways,

00:16:44.030 --> 00:16:48.060
catching you, and defeating you, 
has been my number one goal!

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:50.920
Though they may call me 
the head of this team,

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:53.980
I am an anti, just a simple hunter.

00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:57.270
I will drive out the beast 
known as Ojo Masato!

00:16:58.060 --> 00:16:59.860
I am just a hunter!

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.790
<b>Defense
Souwa / Rokugen</b>

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:05.790
<b>Raider
Noukin / Ojo</b>

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:13.340
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:06.430 --> 00:17:07.240
Learn all you can.

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:11.630
To the best of my knowledge, 
they are the strongest anti and raider.

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.380
It will happen in a flash. 
Burn it into your memory.

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:17.970
Kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:20.830
<i>I've kept you waiting quite 
a while, haven't I...</i>

00:17:20.830 --> 00:17:22.740
<i>It's because you picked a place like Noukin.</i>

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:26.130
<i>Until I became captain, I couldn't 
set up any practice matches.</i>

00:17:28.960 --> 00:17:31.570
<i>You chose a powerhouse school. 
Did anything change?</i>

00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:37.700
<i>That would be a touch, 
if I were who I used to be...</i>

00:17:38.560 --> 00:17:42.580
<i>No, the powerhouse team 
had nothing to do with it!</i>

00:17:42.920 --> 00:17:45.380
<i>I have changed because of you, Ojo!</i>

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.500
<b>Summer, Five Years Earlier
National Middle School Kabaddi Team Selection Practice Venue</b>

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:51.500
<i>I was born with the right build...</i>

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:55.520
<i>Among the selection candidates, 
I stood out conspicuously.</i>

00:17:56.170 --> 00:18:01.660
<i>But in this power-based sport, kabaddi, 
there was one more man who stood out.</i>

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:05.090
Why can't I beat you?

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.390
If I could catch just one finger, 
I could take you down!

00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:10.190
Rokugen, it's because you think like that.

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.920
You rely too much on your strength.

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:15.400
The most important thing is to make 
sure your movements can't be read.

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:21.160
Natural, stable movements come from 
steadily building a foundation.

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:25.000
<i>The man who had been 
born with the slightest build</i>

00:18:25.000 --> 00:18:27.620
<i>continued to hone the weapons 
that remained to him.</i>

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:32.290
<i>The frustration of losing was far 
outweighed by my admiration for him.</i>

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.940
<i>He fought against the weak 
body he'd been given,</i>

00:18:35.940 --> 00:18:38.090
<i>and gained strength. 
If I could beat him, then...</i>

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:41.740
<i>I felt I'd receive something even greater 
than a medal celebrating a win...</i>

00:18:43.570 --> 00:18:46.300
<i>The rough, mud-stained 
medal of a hard worker!</i>

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:48.350
<i>I've got him!</i>

00:18:49.920 --> 00:18:50.820
<i>He dodged?</i>

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:53.150
<i>No! He left his foot there to draw me in?</i>

00:18:53.620 --> 00:18:55.520
Still no struggle.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:57.450
There aren't any openings!

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:58.840
Is his cant gonna hold up?

00:18:58.280 --> 00:19:05.200
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:18:59.390 --> 00:19:02.270
<i>Returning without a touch... 
He wouldn't do that.</i>

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:05.200
<i>Or could it be that his legs
 aren't in their best condition?</i>

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:13.930
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:08.880
Captain Rokugen isn't losing 
out in terms of agility, either!

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:11.210
No, the other guy is really something else!

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:13.930
He injured his legs, didn't he?

00:19:13.930 --> 00:19:16.210
How did he hurt his legs anyway?

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:17.770
<i>Injured?</i>

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:19.520
Kabaddi!

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:22.840
<i>Focus! Stay focused!</i>

00:19:23.060 --> 00:19:25.480
If you play kabaddi, 
you're gonna get injured.

00:19:25.480 --> 00:19:28.690
He's not the kind of guy who'd let 
himself get hurt, though, right?

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:30.850
I can't imagine anyone took him down.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:35.480
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:32.260
<i>Ojo...</i>

00:19:32.260 --> 00:19:35.170
<i>How much have you practiced 
these last three years?</i>

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:38.140
Kabaddi.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:42.920
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:19:38.970 --> 00:19:40.990
<i>You... It can't be that your legs...</i>

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:42.920
<i>that you're the one who...</i>

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:45.310
Kabaddi!

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:48.540
<i>Struggle!</i>

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.290
<i>He came in while I was distracted!</i>

00:19:53.000 --> 00:19:54.890
<i>I will stop you!</i>

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.850
<i>The moment he touches down, the hunt is over!</i>

00:19:57.850 --> 00:19:58.880
<i>H-He's so fast!</i>

00:19:59.360 --> 00:20:00.940
<i>The speed at which he can spin around...</i>

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:12.990
For me, kabaddi is like a beautiful 
woman high up on a pedestal.

00:20:12.990 --> 00:20:15.160
If you don't train yourself 
harder than anyone else,

00:20:15.160 --> 00:20:16.490
she'll never turn to look at you.

00:20:17.600 --> 00:20:20.220
You may be chasing me, but you've 
still got a long ways to go.

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:23.740
The difference between you and me, Rokugen...

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:26.730
is the difference in our love for kabaddi.

00:20:28.630 --> 00:20:29.440
<i>Love?</i>

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:34.670
<b>Noukin: Ojo Raid Successful
Touch 1 pt + Lona 2 pts
 3 pts Gained</b>

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:34.670
Noukin gains three points!

00:20:35.010 --> 00:20:36.630
He did it. They're wiped out...

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:38.380
That's a lona!

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:42.540
D-Don't let it bother you, Rokugen-san.

00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:43.880
What was that?

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:46.390
"That's not good, as a captain," huh?

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:50.390
How does a guy who wrecked his legs through 
overwork have the right to say that?

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:53.740
So, he is that type after all, huh?

00:20:53.740 --> 00:20:56.280
Rokugen-san, you lost, 
but you look pretty happy.

00:20:56.280 --> 00:20:57.400
I'm sorry.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.400
I like that type, too.

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:04.400
And I like sinking them even more.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:07.100
Nice raid, Captain!

00:21:07.100 --> 00:21:08.410
This is just the start!

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:11.320
<i>He wiped them out in just two raids.</i>

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:13.220
<i>The atmosphere is better, too.</i>

00:21:13.220 --> 00:21:14.910
<i>But what is this I'm feeling?</i>

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:18.030
<i>I'm so frustrated!</i>

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:20.680
Don't space out, Yoigoshi!

00:21:20.680 --> 00:21:22.440
They're all back on the court over there!

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:23.800
Takaya's coming!

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:24.880
Right!

00:21:25.160 --> 00:21:27.120
No, there's no need to worry about that.

00:21:27.120 --> 00:21:29.220
Adjustments have been made.

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:30.560
Adjustments?

00:21:30.910 --> 00:21:33.170
That's the end of the first half! Half-time!

00:21:33.170 --> 00:21:34.810
What? Now?

00:21:34.810 --> 00:21:36.060
<i>This isn't good!</i>

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:40.570
<b>Souwa</b>

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:40.570
<b>Noukin</b>

00:21:36.590 --> 00:21:38.210
An eight point spread in the first half.

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:40.570
Though it feels like they took 
a lot more points from us.

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:44.880
If we take the bonus like we did just now,
 and get a lona, we'll be tied.

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:46.570
That seems doable, right?

00:21:48.570 --> 00:21:51.210
<i>The timing of the end of the 
first half works for them...</i>

00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:53.540
<i>Did Ojo deliberately aim for that?</i>

00:21:53.840 --> 00:21:56.500
<i>He didn't have that sort of 
meticulous nature before.</i>

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.650
It's possible to build momentum this way, too.

00:21:58.650 --> 00:22:00.420
Now, let's head to the bench.

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:03.710
Oh, and make sure you all 
look like Yoigoshi...

00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:06.280
like you're sure this 
is gonna be an easy win.

00:22:08.570 --> 00:22:10.280
Those are some nasty expressions.

00:22:10.280 --> 00:22:12.720
Those guys are still losing right now, right?

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:18.380
<i>It's the end of the first half.
Souwa has an eight-point lead, 23 to 15.</i>

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.250
<b>Next Time
"STRUGGLE"</b>

00:23:49.410 --> 00:23:52.550
Kabaddi, kabaddi, kabaddi...

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:51.090
Next time...

00:23:51.090 --> 00:23:51.900
"STRUGGLE"!

00:23:52.550 --> 00:23:53.320
Kabaddi!
